# LSM tree - Log structured merge tree
    - Used for high write throughput (instead of B+ tree)
    - Memtable > SSTable > LSM via compaction
    - In distributed setup, LSM is per node and sharding for a key should be sticky.
# B+ Tree - Used in mysql 
    - Lead node stores actual offset of file which contains rows
    - Good for high read
    - In distributed setup to achive horizontal scaling sharding is the way
    
